WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.066 --> 00:00:00.700
,

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.968 line:78%
MIKE.

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:05.071 line:78%
WE WILL BE FOLLOWING IT TONIGHT.

00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:08.475 line:78%
THANK YOU SO MUCH.

00:00:05.171 --> 00:00:09.175 line:78%
ALSO HERE TONIGHT IS LOUISIANA

00:00:08.575 --> 00:00:12.178 line:78%
SENATOR JOHN KENNEDY, A MEMBER

00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:13.179 line:78%
OF THE JUDICIARY COMMITTEE.

00:00:12.278 --> 00:00:15.148 line:78%
SENATOR, I ALWAYS APPRECIATE

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:16.783 line:78%
YOUR VOICE.

00:00:15.248 --> 00:00:17.517 line:78%
YOU SEEM LIKE A STRAIGHT

00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:19.219 line:78%
SHOOTER, ALWAYS TELLING IT LIKE

00:00:18.852 --> 00:00:23.056 line:78%
IT IS.

00:00:19.319 --> 00:00:24.257 line:78%
WHAT IS THE REPUBLICANS RESPONSE

00:00:23.156 --> 00:00:26.860 line:78%
TO WHAT IS HAPPENING IN AMERICA?

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:29.396 line:78%
BECAUSE IT IS BIPARTISAN.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:31.798 line:78%
WHEN YOU HAVE YOUR COLLEAGUE,

00:00:29.496 --> 00:00:34.234 line:78%
SENATOR TIM SCOTT SAYING HIS

00:00:31.898 --> 00:00:37.470 line:78%
EXPERIENCE, I'M WORRIED THAT

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:39.606 line:78%
AMERICA'S CITIES WILL BURN IF

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:42.642 line:78%
REPUBLICANS DON'T SHOW UP TO

00:00:39.706 --> 00:00:43.743 line:78%
THIS BATTLE, SO WHAT IS THE

00:00:42.742 --> 00:00:45.545 line:78%
RESPONSE?

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:46.713 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, LAWRENCE, HERE'S MY

00:00:45.645 --> 00:00:47.447 line:78%
RESPONSE.

00:00:46.813 --> 00:00:49.516 line:78%
I LISTENED TO YOUR MONOLOGUE.

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:51.818 line:78%
I THOUGHT IT WAS VERY THOUGHTFUL

00:00:49.616 --> 00:00:54.721 line:78%
AND THOUGHT-PROVOKING.

00:00:51.918 --> 00:00:55.455 line:78%
HERE'S MY PERSPECTIVE.

00:00:54.821 --> 00:01:01.628 line:78%
UNLIKE SOME OF MY COLLEAGUES, I

00:00:56.990 --> 00:01:02.295 line:78%
DO NOT BELIEVE THAT AMERICA IS A

00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:04.264 line:78%
RACIST NATION.

00:01:02.595 --> 00:01:06.299 line:78%
WE ARE NOT PERFECT, BUT I THINK

00:01:04.364 --> 00:01:08.468 line:78%
WE ARE GOOD.

00:01:06.599 --> 00:01:10.270 line:78%
NOW, WE HAVE RACISTS IN OUR

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:11.137 line:78%
COUNTRY, JUST LIKE EVERYPLACE

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:11.771 line:78%
ELSE.

00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:13.039 line:78%
THERE ARE PEOPLE IN OUR

00:01:11.871 --> 00:01:15.341 line:78%
COUNTRY -- THERE ARE PEOPLE ALL

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:16.810 line:78%
OVER THE WORLD, LAWRENCE, THAT

00:01:15.442 --> 00:01:17.544 line:78%
ARE GOING TO JUDGE YOU AND NOT

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:19.679 line:78%
LIKE YOU BECAUSE OF THE COLOR OF

00:01:17.644 --> 00:01:20.380 line:78%
YOUR SKIN.

00:01:19.779 --> 00:01:23.183 line:78%
AND THERE ARE OTHERS WHO ARE

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:24.784 line:78%
GOING TO JUDGE ME, THINK THEY

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:25.652 line:78%
KNOW EVERYTHING THEY NEED TO

00:01:24.884 --> 00:01:27.120 line:78%
KNOW ABOUT ME, BECAUSE OF THE

00:01:25.752 --> 00:01:29.722 line:78%
COLOR OF MY SKIN, BUT I DON'T

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:30.457 line:78%
THINK THAT'S MOST AMERICANS.

00:01:29.823 --> 00:01:34.861 line:78%
AND I DON'T THINK THAT'S MOST

00:01:30.557 --> 00:01:36.296 line:78%
COPS IN AMERICA.

00:01:34.961 --> 00:01:36.629 line:78%
WITHOUT ORDER, THERE IS NO

00:01:36.396 --> 00:01:38.064 line:78%
JUSTICE.

00:01:36.796 --> 00:01:41.534 line:78%
WE CAN'T HAVE A SOCIETY WITHOUT

00:01:38.164 --> 00:01:42.235 line:78%
ORDER, AND WE HAVE DECIDED TO

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:45.271 line:78%
HIRE LAW ENFORCEMENT OFFICIALS

00:01:42.335 --> 00:01:46.606 line:78%
TO MAINTAIN ORDER.

00:01:45.371 --> 00:01:54.114 line:78%
WE HIRE WHITES, BLACKS, BROWNS,

00:01:46.706 --> 00:01:56.983 line:78%
MEN, WOMEN, TO MAINTAIN ORDER.

00:01:54.214 --> 00:02:00.053 line:78%
MANY OF OUR LAW ENFORCEMENT

00:01:57.083 --> 00:02:00.854 line:78%
AGENCIES ARE A MAJORITY 

00:02:00.153 --> 00:02:02.922 line:78%
MINORITY.

00:02:00.954 --> 00:02:03.756 line:78%
AND IF YOU DECIDE, JUST LIKE YOU

00:02:03.022 --> 00:02:04.757 line:78%
WANT TO JUDGE SOMEONE SOLELY BY

00:02:03.857 --> 00:02:07.660 line:78%
THE COLOR OF THE SKIN, IF YOU

00:02:04.858 --> 00:02:10.697 line:78%
WANT TO MAKE A PEJORATIVE

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:12.565 line:78%
JUDGMENT ABOUT A COP, I'LL PUT

00:02:10.797 --> 00:02:13.967 line:78%
IT THIS WAY, IF YOU HATE COPS

00:02:12.665 --> 00:02:15.835 line:78%
JUST BECAUSE THEY ARE COPS, YOU

00:02:14.067 --> 00:02:16.803 line:78%
DON'T KNOW A THING ABOUT THEM,

00:02:15.935 --> 00:02:18.872 line:78%
THE NEXT TIME YOU GET IN

00:02:16.903 --> 00:02:22.008 line:78%
TROUBLE, CALL A CRACKHEAD.

00:02:18.972 --> 00:02:25.345 line:78%
NOW, HAVING SAID THAT, WHAT WE

00:02:22.108 --> 00:02:26.079 line:78%
ARE REALLY TALKING ABOUT HERE,

00:02:25.445 --> 00:02:28.748 line:78%
WHAT WE ARE TALKING ABOUT HERE

00:02:26.179 --> 00:02:30.950 line:78%
IS THE RELATIONSHIP BETWEEN

00:02:28.848 --> 00:02:33.153 line:78%
CRIME AND RACE.

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:35.555 line:78%
LET'S JUST CUT TO THE CHASE.

00:02:33.253 --> 00:02:38.725 line:78%
IT IS A STATISTICAL FACT THAT

00:02:35.655 --> 00:02:41.461 line:78%
JUST AS IT IS THE CASE THAT MORE

00:02:38.825 --> 00:02:44.664 line:78%
MEN THAN WOMEN COMMIT CRIMES,

00:02:41.561 --> 00:02:45.932 line:78%
JUST AS IT IS A STATISTICAL FACT

00:02:44.764 --> 00:02:49.903 line:78%
THAT MORE YOUNGER PEOPLE THAN

00:02:46.032 --> 00:02:50.870 line:78%
OLDER PEOPLE COMMIT CRIMES, WE

00:02:50.003 --> 00:02:52.071 line:78%
HAVE RACIAL MINORITIES AND

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:54.941 line:78%
ETHNIC GROUPS IN AMERICA THAT

00:02:52.172 --> 00:02:57.043 line:78%
HAVE HIGHER CRIME RATES.

00:02:55.041 --> 00:02:57.944 line:78%
WHY?

00:02:57.143 --> 00:03:00.146 line:78%
POVERTY.

00:02:58.044 --> 00:03:00.513 line:78%
BUT THAT DOESN'T TELL YOU

00:03:00.246 --> 00:03:01.347 line:78%
ANYTHING.

00:03:00.613 --> 00:03:04.117 line:78%
HOW DO WE STOP POVERTY?

00:03:01.447 --> 00:03:05.251 line:78%
I DON'T KNOW A SINGLE PERSON WHO

00:03:04.217 --> 00:03:06.686 line:78%
IS POOR WHO WANTS TO BE POOR.

00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:07.520 line:78%
&gt;&gt; Lawrence: THE PROBLEM,

00:03:06.786 --> 00:03:09.722 line:78%
SENATOR, WE HAVE TO GET TO THE

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:11.491 line:78%
ROOT CAUSES OF CRIME.

00:03:09.822 --> 00:03:13.026 line:78%
BUT EVEN IF -- I LOVE WHEN YOU

00:03:11.591 --> 00:03:13.326 line:78%
SAY LAW AND ORDER BECAUSE IT IS

00:03:13.126 --> 00:03:15.662 line:78%
TRUE.

00:03:13.426 --> 00:03:16.095 line:78%
A NATION WITHOUT LAW AND

00:03:15.762 --> 00:03:17.931 line:78%
ORDER --

00:03:16.196 --> 00:03:18.831 line:78%
BUT EVEN WITHIN THAT LAW, THERE

00:03:18.164 --> 00:03:19.599 line:78%
IS DUE PROCESS.

00:03:18.932 --> 00:03:23.136 line:78%
DUE PROCESS FOR THE PEOPLE THAT

00:03:19.699 --> 00:03:26.005 line:78%
COMMIT THOSE CRIMES, AND DUE

00:03:23.236 --> 00:03:26.739 line:78%
PROCESS FOR THE LAW ENFORCEMENT

00:03:26.105 --> 00:03:27.073 line:78%
OFFICERS THAT HAVE TO CONFRONT

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:28.374 line:78%
THOSE --

00:03:27.907 --> 00:03:29.709 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, THAT'S TRUE.

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:30.677 line:78%
&gt;&gt; Lawrence: IT IS ONE THING

00:03:29.809 --> 00:03:33.446 line:78%
TO CONFRONT THE CRIME, WHICH WE

00:03:30.777 --> 00:03:34.881 line:78%
HAVE TO DO AS AMERICANS.

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:35.648 line:78%
AND SUPPORT THE LAW ENFORCEMENT

00:03:34.981 --> 00:03:36.749 line:78%
OFFICERS THAT DO THAT.

00:03:35.748 --> 00:03:37.850 line:78%
BUT WHEN YOU SHOW UP TO THE

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:39.285 line:78%
SCENE OF A CRIME AND THE

00:03:37.951 --> 00:03:41.054 line:78%
CITIZENS OF THIS COUNTRY HAVE

00:03:39.385 --> 00:03:43.356 line:78%
GIVEN YOU THAT RESPONSIBILITY,

00:03:41.154 --> 00:03:46.259 line:78%
AND YOU HAVE A BAD SHOOT, THERE

00:03:43.456 --> 00:03:48.461 line:78%
HAS TO BE A PROCESS -- WHICH WE

00:03:46.359 --> 00:03:49.295 line:78%
HAVE A LEGAL PROCESS, BUT

00:03:48.661 --> 00:03:53.733 line:78%
REPUBLICANS HAVE NOT RESPONDED

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:54.167 line:78%
TO THAT.

00:03:53.833 --> 00:03:56.035 line:78%
&gt;&gt; RESPOND --

00:03:54.267 --> 00:03:57.437 line:78%
&gt;&gt; Lawrence: IT CAN'T JUST BE

00:03:56.135 --> 00:03:58.571 line:78%
"THERE IS CRIME IN AMERICA."

00:03:57.537 --> 00:04:00.206 line:78%
CRIME IS ALWAYS GOING TO EXIST,

00:03:58.972 --> 00:04:01.107 line:78%
WE HAVE TO DEAL WITH AT.

00:04:00.306 --> 00:04:04.911 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I CAN GIVE YOU TWO THINGS WE

00:04:01.207 --> 00:04:07.347 line:78%
CAN DO TO REDUCE THE CRIME RATE

00:04:05.011 --> 00:04:08.114 line:78%
AMONG ALL DEMOGRAPHIC GROUPS,

00:04:07.447 --> 00:04:08.715 line:78%
BUT ESPECIALLY AMONG

00:04:08.214 --> 00:04:09.649 line:78%
AFRICAN-AMERICAN YOUTHS.

00:04:08.815 --> 00:04:13.453 line:78%
NUMBER ONE, WE ARE SENDING

00:04:09.749 --> 00:04:15.955 line:78%
2 MILLION OF OUR YOUNG PEOPLE TE

00:04:13.553 --> 00:04:17.590 line:78%
FAILURE FACTORIES.

00:04:16.055 --> 00:04:19.525 line:78%
LET ME TELL YOU, IF I WORKING

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:19.792 line:78%
FOR A DAY, HERE IS WHAT I WOULD

00:04:19.626 --> 00:04:24.230 line:78%
DO.

00:04:21.494 --> 00:04:27.133 line:78%
I WOULD TURN TO ALL OF THE

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:29.769 line:78%
PARENTS OF OUR KIDS BELOW A

00:04:27.233 --> 00:04:31.371 line:78%
CERTAIN SOCIAL ECONOMIC LEVEL,

00:04:29.869 --> 00:04:33.573 line:78%
OF ALL RACES, AND I'D SAY "HERE

00:04:31.471 --> 00:04:34.807 line:78%
IS THE MONEY THAT THE STATE IS

00:04:33.673 --> 00:04:35.875 line:78%
PUTTING UP TO PAY FOR THE SCHOOL

00:04:34.907 --> 00:04:37.610 line:78%
YOU ARE GOING TO.

00:04:35.975 --> 00:04:38.511 line:78%
I'M GIVING YOU THE MONEY, NOT

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.712 line:78%
THE SCHOOL.

00:04:38.611 --> 00:04:41.481 line:78%
USE IT ANYWHERE YOU WANT TO.

00:04:39.812 --> 00:04:41.881 line:78%
YOU WANT TO GO TO A CHARTER

00:04:41.581 --> 00:04:43.049 line:78%
SCHOOL, GO.

00:04:41.981 --> 00:04:45.852 line:78%
YOU WANT TO GO TO A PRIVATE

00:04:43.149 --> 00:04:48.154 line:78%
SCHOOL, HERE'S THE MONEY."

00:04:45.952 --> 00:04:50.323 line:78%
WE HAVE TO HAVE MORE FREEDOM OF

00:04:48.254 --> 00:04:50.823 line:78%
CHOICE AND MORE COMPETITION IN

00:04:50.556 --> 00:04:53.293 line:78%
EDUCATION.

00:04:50.923 --> 00:04:54.894 line:78%
NUMBER TWO, FAMILY FORMATION.

00:04:53.393 --> 00:04:56.262 line:78%
NOBODY WANTS TO TALK ABOUT IT.

00:04:54.994 --> 00:04:58.865 line:78%
I'M NOT SAYING A SINGLE PARENT

00:04:56.362 --> 00:05:00.867 line:78%
CAN'T BE A GOOD MOM OR DAD, BUT

00:04:58.965 --> 00:05:02.268 line:78%
A CHILD WHO GROWS UP IN A

00:05:00.967 --> 00:05:04.704 line:78%
SINGLE-PARENT FAMILY IS SIX

00:05:02.368 --> 00:05:05.872 line:78%
TIMES MORE LIKELY TO GROW UP IN

00:05:04.804 --> 00:05:08.074 line:78%
POVERTY AND A CHILD THAT GROWS

00:05:05.972 --> 00:05:15.415 line:78%
UP IN A TWO PARENT FAMILY.

00:05:08.174 --> 00:05:15.982 line:78%
AND THAT IS JUST A FACT.

00:05:15.515 --> 00:05:16.683 line:78%
&gt;&gt; Lawrence: YOU KNOW,

00:05:16.082 --> 00:05:17.383 line:78%
SENATOR, I HAVE BEEN VOCAL, I

00:05:16.783 --> 00:05:18.284 line:78%
HAVE BEEN FIGHTING FOR SCHOOL

00:05:17.483 --> 00:05:20.019 line:78%
CHOICE MY ENTIRE CAREER.

00:05:18.384 --> 00:05:21.788 line:78%
AND SO I SUPPORT YOU ON THAT,

00:05:20.119 --> 00:05:25.058 line:78%
BUT I LOOK FORWARD TO SEEING THE

00:05:21.888 --> 00:05:26.059 line:78%
REPUBLICANS FORM A RESPONSE.

00:05:25.158 --> 00:05:27.493 line:78%
TIM SCOTT HAD A BILL, BUT THAT

00:05:26.159 --> 00:05:28.761 line:78%
IS A FEDERAL BILL.

00:05:27.593 --> 00:05:30.163 line:78%
I WANT TO SEE SOMETHING ON THE

00:05:28.861 --> 00:05:30.163 line:78%
LOCAL LEVEL, AND I WILL INVITE

